From: "A.Cervantez" <155030226+Ywach404@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:06:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] runtime: step answers with the left stick and mark a lone
 answer

On device the selector worked, but the thumb that reaches for it is
the left one, the stick that walks. In dialogue mode the left stick's
up and down flicks now step the highlight with the same repeat the
right stick has. The right stick keeps stepping: look is off in a
dialogue, so it does no harm. Both sticks share the four flick
buttons, so one controls.txt line moves both and live() still fits a
pad in 32 bits. A held flick stays with the stick that fired it, so
the other stick cannot take it over mid push. Walking and stepping
are gated by the same mode test, so a push in a dialogue is never
both. After a dialogue opens each stick has to centre once before it
steps, as the right one did.

A dialogue with one answer now has it marked as soon as it shows, so
Cross or RT confirms it with no step; one answer is what continue is
in this HUD. The check runs every pump, so a pick that leads to a
one-answer node is marked too, and a Cross that soon still waits out
the 0.5 s guard. Two answers or more stay unmarked until the first
move. Two sets are left alone: the one Circle cleared, until the
answers change or the dialogue closes, and the one a confirm just
picked, until the game's pick time moves or the answers change, so
the line still on screen is not marked again and copied into the
history with its marker. Only while a pad drives a dialogue: under a
menu, or for a keyboard player, the game's own text is left as is.
